      },
      "message": "fix(ui): native dialogs are owned by the shell window (#1067)\n\nEvery picker was built without an owner, so Windows could put the Open or\nSave dialog behind the app; a shell launched from a terminal was not the\nforeground window either, so the first dialog of a session was the worst\ncase.\n\nPublish the shell window once it exists (a thread-local: winit's Window is\n!Send), hand it to rfd with set_parent, and raise it just before a picker\nopens. The shell also asks for the foreground once at startup, and the GPU\nrefusal MessageDialog is owned the same way.\n\nHand-checked on Windows 11 at 125 %: launch from a terminal, first Ctrl+O,\nthe #32770 \"Open\" dialog is topmost and visible. No headless test: rfd\nmodals are hand-test-only here.\n\nFixes #1067",
